u0027m focusing on defining the real form of an opiate.\n\n\n**Defining the Digital Opiate**\n\nI\u0027ve shifted my focus to Kevyn\u0027s digital \"cavern.\" It\u0027s clear that it is his meticulous memory, not forgetting, that represents the true opiate, paralyzing him. I\u0027m building on the contrast: true forgetting enables creation, like a child playing freely, while excessive memory, like Kevyn\u0027s Obsidian archive, is a burden. I\u0027m formulating an analogy of the child and the \"forgetting\" that frees it. I am working on how Kevyn\u0027s obsession with the past has envenomed his intellect.\n\n\n**Embracing the Liberation**\n\nI see \"Assim foi\" as the central burden, the past Kevyn endlessly ruminates. My proposed redemption is transforming that into \"Assim eu quis!\" This represents active digestion, not passive amnesia. Kevyn doesn\u0027t digest; he embalms his traumas, the digital archive. He\u0027s urged to put the theory into practice and wake up without the weight of his past, to step outside his glass dome.\n\n\n",
